## THE COMMISSION (RELAYED)
The product owner ruled the card `hpsmpoc-class-c-wording-six-tickets-1022` on the live board at 2026-10-22 16:41:45 AEDT, verbatim: *"Decision hpsmpoc-class-c-wording-six-tickets-1022: a — Approve the recommended set"*. The set (RELAYED by Tuesday's commission): `148 b · 177 a · 178 a · 187 a · 204 b · 310: 3b 4a 5a 6a 7a 8a`. This brief builds **177 a and 178 a**. 148 and 310 are brief B465 (web); 187, 204 and the records are brief B467 (Reporting). Nothing here needs HP or a human outside the team.

### 177 a (exact words)
Refuse, in the feedback comment, the same set that follow-up notes refuse (ruling C-36 C): U+E0000 to U+E007F (the TAG block), U+2028, U+2029, U+FEFF, U+FFF9 to U+FFFC, U+206A to U+206F, plus the control characters and text-direction overrides already refused. **Kept allowed** (real text needs them): zero-width joiner U+200D and non-joiner U+200C, no-break space U+00A0, soft hyphen U+00AD, U+200B, U+2060 to U+2064, and line feed, carriage return and tab. The refusal keeps the code `feedback.comment-invalid` (field `comment`) and its message becomes, exactly:
`The comment holds a hidden control or text-direction character (often from copying and pasting); type it again as plain text.`
(Today: `The comment holds control or text-direction characters.`) The web shows the API's first message as it is (`web/src/components/feedback/feedbackApi.ts:58`), so no web change is needed (re-read it and say so).

### 178 a (exact words)
Refuse the C-36 C set plus control and text-direction characters in a customer name, on create AND on rename. New code `customer.name-invalid`, field `name`, message exactly:
`The name holds a hidden control or text-direction character (often from copying and pasting); type it again as plain text.`
Today there is no refusal: the name is checked only for length 1 to 120 (`name takes 1 to 120 characters.`) and not blank (`name is blank.`); a name with U+202E, a TAG character, a byte-order mark or BEL is stored, and the client sees it as `For <customer name>`. The web mock's customer create and rename must refuse the same way (mock parity, as follow-up notes have it).

